 null, "schedule_impact_days": null}, {"title": "Regarding post install anchor at building-2.", "answer": "Anchor bolts have not been installed", "status": "Closed", "priority": "Medium", "question": "NOTE#1:- As per the AOR snap, we have kept a slab edge around the future stair opening. Due \n                 to this, we are required to shift the column at 2'-4\" from Grid A.1 towards Grid-B \n                 (refer  to Snap-1). Please note that this column is extending up to the roof level.\n\n                 Since the anchor bolts have already been cast, we will need to provide a post-\n                 installed anchor arrangement at this location. The proposed arrangement for the post-\n                 installed anchors is shown in Snap-2 & 3. \n\n                 Please confirm if this is a", "discipline": "Structural", "rfi_number": "RFI #055", "answered_by": "Nick Lortz", "assigned_to": "LGE", "cost_impact": false, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": "2026-05-23", "date_required": "2026-05-29", "submitted_date": "2026-05-22", "schedule_impact": false, "drawing_reference": null, "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": null}, {"title": "Regarding Wedge Canopy Frame at Corners of Building", "answer": "", "status": "Closed", "priority": "Medium", "question": "NOTE#1:- After incorporating the BFA comments, the wedge canopy arrangement at the \n                 clouded corner-1 & corner-2 is appearing as shown in the attached references.\n\n                 A. For corner-1 the arrangement shown in Snap-1 is for Level-2, and \n                     the arrangement shown in Snap-2 is for the lower roof level.\n\n                 B. For corner-2 the arrangement shown in Snap-3 is for Level-2, and \n                     the arrangement shown in Snap-4 is for the lower roof level.\n\n                  Please review and confirm whether the proposed arrangement is ac", "discipline": "Structural", "rfi_number": "RFI #056", "answered_by": null, "assigned_to": "LGE", "cost_impact": false, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": null, "date_required": "2026-06-01", "submitted_date": "2026-05-26", "schedule_impact": true, "drawing_reference": "Structurals", "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": 5}, {"title": "Regarding Stabilizer Plate Angle for Joists", "answer": "Proceed with 6x6x1/4\"", "status": "Closed", "priority": "Medium", "question": "NOTE#1:- There is a conflict between the joist drawing and the design drawing:\n\n                 A. In Section 13/S105 of the design drawing, an L3x3x1/4 angle is provided to  \n                     stabilize the bottom leg of the joist.\n\n                 B. However, in Sections 5 and 9 of the joist drawing, a stabilizer plate is specified.\n\n                 Currently, we are following the joist drawing and providing a stabilizer plate \n                 (PL 3/4\" x 6\" x 6\").\n\n                 Please confirm whether we are proceeding correctly or advise if any changes are \n                 requir", "discipline": "Structural", "rfi_number": "RFI #057", "answered_by": "New Mill / S&H", "assigned_to": "LGE", "cost_impact": false, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": "2026-05-27", "date_required": "2026-06-01", "submitted_date": "2026-05-26", "schedule_impact": true, "drawing_reference": null, "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": 5}, {"title": "Column Shift for Self-Closing Gate Clearance", "answer": "", "status": "Closed", "priority": "Medium", "question": "Per the RFI #45 response, the roof ladder height exceeds 30'-0\", requiring the second-floor balcony to serve as an intermediate landing with a 3'-0\" self-closing gate at the guardrail. To create the required gate opening at the Building-1 balcony, the column must shift north as shown on Sheet 601E123.", "discipline": "Structural", "rfi_number": "RFI #058", "answered_by": "Nick Lortz", "assigned_to": "LGE", "cost_impact": false, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": "2026-06-16", "date_required": "2026-06-23", "submitted_date": "2026-06-16", "schedule_impact": true, "drawing_reference": "601E123", "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": 1}, {"title": "Joist Splice Connection Bolts", "answer": "Proceed with TC", "status": "Closed", "priority": "Medium", "question": "IFC drawings detail shows joist splice connection made with A490 hex head bolts.\nS&H Steel requests to furnish and install tension control (TC) bolts at all bolted joists and joist girder field\nsplice connections, in lieu of standard hex structural bolts.S&H proposes the following assembly:\n- ASTM Grade F2280 (TC, A490-equivalent).\nPlease confirm that TC bolts are acceptable for the field splice connection.\nOnce a response has been received from New Mill, a copy will be forwarded to the GC/AOR/EOR for record.", "discipline": "Connections", "rfi_number": "RFI #059", "answered_by": "New Mill", "assigned_to": "New Mill", "cost_impact": true, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": "2026-06-19", "date_required": "2026-06-22", "submitted_date": "2026-06-18", "schedule_impact": false, "drawing_reference": "J1", "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": null}, {"title": "Regarding hangar door post brace support arrangement at building-2.", "answer": "", "status": "Under Review", "priority": "Medium", "question": "NOTE#1:- At the clouded location, the angle brace arrangement intended to support the hanger\n                 post is not feasible over the joist, because the joist is terminating before reaching the\n                 face of the return panel.\n                Therefore, we have provided the brace support arrangement directly on the concrete\n                panel using a 1/2\" thick plate with TITEN HD screw anchor, as shown in Snap-1 and\n                Snap-2.\n                Please confirm whether this connection, as shown in Snap-1 and Snap-2, is\n                acceptable. If not, please sug", "discipline": "Structural", "rfi_number": "RFI #060", "answered_by": null, "assigned_to": "LGE", "cost_impact": false, "ball_in_court": "GC", "date_answered": null, "date_required": "2026-06-25", "submitted_date": "2026-06-18", "schedule_impact": true, "drawing_reference": null, "cost_impact_amount": null, "schedule_impact_days": null}]